{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And every woman who has known a man — for lying with a male, kill.</b> Rashi explained: why did he repeat and say 'kill,' etc. And if you ask: if it were so that they were permitted to keep alive every woman who had known a man, then 'and all the female children among the women who have not known,' etc., would be superfluous — now it is a fortiori: if women who have known a man were permitted to live, certainly female children! One may answer: had it not written 'and all the female children among the women,' etc., I might have derived 'female children' from 'male children' (טף בנשים מטף בזכר): just as there, to kill, so too here, to kill. Another interpretation: <b>kill</b> — why is it stated? If she is capable of intercourse, [the command] to kill [applies] to one who has already been lain with, all the more so [to one who is capable but has not yet been lain with]. Rather, if you say so, you have punished [her] by strict law; therefore it says <b>kill</b> — that one does not punish by strict law. And if you ask: let the verse be silent about the first 'kill' and write thus: 'and now, every male and every woman who has known a man,' etc.? [Answer:] if it were written thus, one might think to spare all the male children and not kill them until we pass them before women before the frontplate (ציץ) and kill them together with them. Therefore it says <b>and now kill every male among the children</b> — that is, now, immediately, kill every male among the children; <b>and every woman who has known a man</b> — after she has been examined by the frontplate, kill her. [And every woman who has known a man — it is the way of the world that a man seduces the woman; but the daughters of Midian, who were wanton and seduced Israel, the verse states of them 'and every woman who has known a man.']"], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:25.440886204Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}